{
  "title": "Seymour Fracture",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6000/seymour-fracture",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 24 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "5",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Seymour Fractures are displaced distal phalangeal physeal fractures with an associated nailbed injury.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with the presence of nail plate lying superficial to the eponychial fold and radiographs potentially showing widened physis or displacement between the epiphysis and metaphysis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually antibiotics, open reduction and pinning across DIPJ with nailbed repair.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "20% to 30% of phalangeal fractures involve the physis in children",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "middle finger injury is most common",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**type of the distal phalangeal physeal fracture**:",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "metaphyseal fractures 1 to 2 mm distal to the epiphyseal plate",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Salter-Harris I fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Salter-Harris II fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**type of nailbed injury:**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "nailbed laceration",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "nail plate subluxation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "interposition of soft tissue at fracture site (usually germinal matrix)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism of injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "direct trauma or crush injury (e.g. caught in door, heavy object or sport)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "similar mechanism to mallet finger in adults",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "injury causes flexed posturing of the distal phalanx",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "deformity results from an imbalance between the flexor and the extensor tendons at the level of the fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "imbalance occurs due to different insertion sites of flexor and extensor tendons",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "extensor tendon inserts into the **epiphysis of the distal phalanx**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "flexor tendon inserts into **metaphysis of the distal phalanx**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "widened physis likely to have interposed tissue in the fracture site",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "apparent mallet deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "echymosis and swelling",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "nail plate lying superficial to the eponychial fold",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "PA",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "may appear normal",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "lateral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "widened physis or displacement between epiphysis/metaphysis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6000/images/seymourap.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "flexion deformity at fracture site",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6000/images/smimages.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "seen on lateral view",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "4",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mallet finger",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pediatric mallet finger is usually osseous avulsion (SH III and SH IV)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "mallet finger fracture line enters DIPJ, while Seymour fracture line traverses physis (does not enter DIPJ)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "closed reduction and splinting",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "minimally displaced, closed fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "no interposition of soft tissue at fracture site",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "closed reduction and pinning across DIPJ",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "displaced, closed fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "no interposition of soft tissue at fracture site",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**open reduction and pinning across DIPJ, nailbed repair**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**open management has fewer complications than closed management**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "open fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "hyperflexion of the digit will permit removal of the interposed soft tissue from the fracture site",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "thorough irrigation and debridement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "anatomical reduction and retrograde k-wire fixation crossing the fracture site and DIP joint",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "nailbed injury repair",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Nail dystrophy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Growth disturbance of the distal phalanx and nail**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Secondary fracture displacement**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Chronic osteomyelitis (failure to treat as open fracture)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Flexion deformity**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Operative intervention is warranted to ensure that there is no interposed tissue in the fracture site",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Failure to recognize injury may result in:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "nailplate deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "physeal arrest",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "chronic osteomyelitis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
